              "id": "text-14",
              "kind": "text",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Titanium Grade 3 CP 2 | UNS #R50550 offers slightly higher mechanical properties than Grade 2 Titanium. Grade 3 demonstrates similar ductility and formability, however. This metal is typically used for applications where corrosion resistance is a major requirement and largely used in chemical production, some airframe applications, and marine use."
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 2,
                  "text": "Titanium Sheet Grade 3 CP 2 Specifications:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[AMS 4900](https://titanium.com/ams-4900-titanium-grade-3/) , [AMS-T-9046 CP 2](https://titanium.com/ams-t-9046-specification/)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[ASTM B265](https://titanium.com/astm-b265-specification/) , [ASTM F67](https://titanium.com/astm-f67-specification/)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "EN 10204.3.1, [ASME SB-265](https://titanium.com/asme-sb265-specification/)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Titanium Grade 3 Mill Product Forms:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[Grade 3 Titanium Sheet](https://qqa.titanium.com/product/mill-product-titanium-sheet)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
